   "video_id": "819019799"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Laws of logarithms"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are the laws of logarithms?"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/07/6.2.1-Laws-of-Logarithms-Notes-fig1.png",
   "file": "assets/f463b06c8290-6-2-1-laws-of-logarithms-notes-fig1.png",
   "alt": "Laws of Logarithms Notes fig1, A Level & AS Maths: Pure revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- There are many laws or rules of indices, for example\n\n  - **a**<sup>**m**</sup>** x a**<sup>**n**</sup>** = a**<sup>**m+n**</sup>\n  - **(a**<sup>**m**</sup>**)**<sup>**n**</sup>** = a**<sup>**mn**</sup>\n- There are equivalent laws of logarithms (for a > 0)\n\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}xy=\\mathrm{log}_{a}x+\\mathrm{log}_{a}y$\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}(\\frac{x}{y})=\\mathrm{log}_{a}x-\\mathrm{log}_{a}y$\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}x^{k}=k\\mathrm{log}_{a}x$"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/6.2.1-Laws-of-Logarithms-Notes-fig2.png",
   "file": "assets/b3870da6fd3f-6-2-1-laws-of-logarithms-notes-fig2.png",
   "alt": "Laws of Logarithms Notes fig2, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- There are also some particular results these lead to\n\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}a=1$\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}a^{x}=x$\n  - $a^{\\mathrm{log}_{a}x}=x$\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}1=0$\n  - $\\mathrm{log}_{a}(\\frac{1}{x})=-\\mathrm{log}_{a}x$"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/6.2.1-Laws-of-Logarithms-Notes-fig3.png",
   "file": "assets/c9b61f5fe62a-6-2-1-laws-of-logarithms-notes-fig3.png",
   "alt": "Laws of Logarithms Notes fig3, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Two of these were seen in the notes Logarithmic Functions\n- Beware …\n\n  - … **log (x + y) ≠ log x + log y**\n- Results apply to** ln **too\n\n  - $\\mathrm{ln}x\\equiv\\mathrm{log}_{e}x$\n  - In particular $e^{\\mathrm{ln}x}=x$ and $\\mathrm{ln}(e^{x})=x$"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I use log laws?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Laws of logarithms can be used to … ![Laws of Logarithms Notes fig4, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes](assets/e87d814c47bc-6-2-1-laws-of-logarithms-notes-fig4.png)\n\n  - … simplify expressions\n  - … solve logarithmic equations\n  - … solve exponential equations"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "- Remember to check whether your solutions are valid. log (x+k) is only defined if x > -k.\n- You will lose marks if you forget to reject invalid solutions."
  },
